# Dawnhand Dissident's "{T}, Blight 2: Exile target card from a graveyard" may put the counters on the Dissident itself, though it
# dies of them (the ruling: the creature "doesn't have to have enough toughness to survive the process", CR 704.5f). The ability
# is independent of its source once activated (CR 113.7a), so Bot1's Llanowar Elves are still exiled. But the permission to cast
# them is a static ability of the Dissident, which no longer exists (CR 113.6, 611.3a): with three +1/+1 counters on a Walking
# Ballista and {G} open, the Elves can't be cast from exile. The twin that casts them is
# "...exiles-a-creature-and-casts-it-removing-counters-of-two-kinds".

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Dawnhand Dissident
Llanowar Elves
Walking Ballista
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x18

